            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0409" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-26T18:00:00-04:00">July 26, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Your July 24, 10 p.m. Regarding Section 2 of the Liberian proposal is there
                    any other law which could, if necessary, be invoked by the commission in order
                    to strengthen its hand in dealing with witnesses.</p>
                <p>Please cable reply with your comments and suggestions following which the
                    Department will instruct you further.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
